title: BitLocker Abused to Lock Out Data
id: 114af2c0-cd44-4c03-a947-73e0596a1ade
status: experimental
description: Detects attacker use of manage-bde or Enable-BitLocker to encrypt volumes with an attacker-held key, a technique that abuses the built-in disk encryption to lock victims out of their data without ransomware binaries.
author: Alaris Global
references:
  - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1486/
logsource:
  product: windows
  category: process_creation
detection:
  selection:
    CommandLine|contains:
      - 'manage-bde'
      - 'Enable-BitLocker'
    CommandLine|contains:
      - '-on'
      - '-EncryptionMethod'
      - '-RecoveryPassword'
      - '-Password'
  condition: selection
fields:
  - CommandLine
  - Image
  - ParentImage
falsepositives:
  - Legitimate BitLocker deployment
level: high
tags:
  - attack.impact
  - attack.t1486
